#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059528 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "8369943c-d7d8-5b77-949b-b48a4a4a96d1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5780" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b$." :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1-\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $1+\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1+\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} &=\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {1 + \\textrm{i}} {1 + \\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {4 + 4\\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i}^2} {1^2 - \\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {4 + 5\\textrm{i} + (-1)} {1 - (-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+\\textrm{i} b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} = \\dfrac{3} {2} + \\dfrac {5} {2} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/id #uuid "107d76c0-349a-549d-adeb-f009492cd79c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5781" :question/problem "If $z_1 = -8-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2\\textrm{i}$, then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $2\\textrm{i}$. Note that this can be written as $0+2\\textrm{i}$, so the conjugate is $0-2\\textrm{i}$, or simply $-2\\textrm{i}$.\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} &= \\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-2\\textrm{i}} {-2\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6\\textrm{i}^2} {-4\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6(-1)} {-4(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} &=-\\dfrac{6}{4} + \\dfrac{16}{4} \\textrm{i} \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{3} {2} + 4\\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/id #uuid "74740363-2309-5680-9373-05ce0fed9bcf" :question/math-academy-id "e-6230" :question/problem "If $z_1=3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2+5\\textrm{i}$, then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3\\textrm{i}}{2+5\\textrm i}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $2+5\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $2-5\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2-5\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5\\textrm{i}} &= \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {2 -5 \\textrm{i}} {2-5\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15 \\textrm{i}^2} {2^2 - (5\\textrm{i})^2} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15\\textrm{i}^2} {4 - 25\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15(-1)} {4 - 25(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15} {29} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15} {29}= \\dfrac{15} {29} + \\dfrac {6} {29} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059531 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/id #uuid "2fc036dd-7732-50ed-adef-8c37bd87fecd" :question/math-academy-id "e-6231" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{4}{-1+2\\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b$." :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-1+2\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $-1-2\\textrm{i}$. We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-1-2\\textrm{i}$, so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {4} {-1 +2\\textrm{i}} &=\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-1 -2 \\textrm{i}} {-1-2\\textrm{i}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {(-1)^2 - (2\\textrm{i})^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {1 - 4\\textrm{i}^2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {1 - 4(-1)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {5} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i}} {5} = -\\dfrac{4} {5} - \\dfrac {8} {5} \\textrm{i} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9d0d6b4-6b8f-5458-902e-67cb5e0eb4c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265107} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe6ef84-836f-5264-bccb-870431f66b2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{36}{41}+\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265108} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b1c68c-2457-5713-bdcb-4ed40192cd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{36}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265109} {:answer/id #uuid "83179840-dd1b-5e72-954a-533df91cf8e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265110} {:answer/id #uuid "04149162-d45f-5ad5-a5c8-096244656e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{41}+\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83179840-dd1b-5e72-954a-533df91cf8e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265110} :answer-field/id #uuid "7da19a51-57ce-5e7d-aa31-27661ae89e41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265106}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e9471e3-3f65-5f76-b938-80f99b825051" :question/math-academy-id "q-16433" :question/problem "$\\frac{9\\text{i}}{-5+4\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-5+4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-5-4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-5-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9\\text{i}}{-5+4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{9\\text{i}}{-5+4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-5-4\\text{i}}{-5-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-45\\text{i}-36{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{5}^{2}-{4}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-45\\text{i}-36(-1)}{{5}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36-45\\text{i}}{25+16} \\\\  & =\\frac{36-45\\text{i}}{41}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{36-45\\text{i}}{41}=\\frac{36}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59d3d44f-d9b4-542e-9cac-be461f2010af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265114} {:answer/id #uuid "6842d239-7e28-50a9-829f-abb73b8f2594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{4}{3}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265115} {:answer/id #uuid "f7bd2787-be10-5f08-971d-d6352b08b037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265116} {:answer/id #uuid "3763f200-ca3d-50c3-8bbc-11aba2f53880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265117} {:answer/id #uuid "24b85aa9-506b-568d-a828-429d5de70927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3763f200-ca3d-50c3-8bbc-11aba2f53880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265117} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fad7d82-e734-5818-b622-1f31abb5c496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265113}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84548505-14f7-5f3f-bcde-d25a5f7698d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-167670" :question/problem "$\\frac{-3-4\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1-\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1+\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1+\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3-4\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-3-4\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-3\\text{i}-4\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-7\\text{i}-4(-1)}{1-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-7\\text{i}+4}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-7\\text{i}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-7\\text{i}}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}\\text{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3c49c91-4312-5bda-877f-f3e286384d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265121} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1d726c-6e0e-5cdc-8852-edb88bca4e10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{5}{2}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265122} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd4c821-cdf8-5a5a-a219-e865dd617675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265123} {:answer/id #uuid "c00eaf42-edf5-5382-b2df-b701ce6b0bb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265124} {:answer/id #uuid "df98f873-a479-55a8-b851-41a7fefd6130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df98f873-a479-55a8-b851-41a7fefd6130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265125} :answer-field/id #uuid "5df39a8b-f28c-5b14-add8-7b719a71abda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265120}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffce566e-b201-5edb-874f-34eee0332074" :question/math-academy-id "q-167677" :question/problem "$\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{5\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $5\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+5\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-5\\text{i},$ or simply $-5\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-5\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{5\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{5\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-5\\text{i}}{-5\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-25\\text{i}-10{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-25{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-25\\text{i}-10(-1)}{-25(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-25\\text{i}}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10-25\\text{i}}{25} & =\\frac{10}{25}-\\frac{25}{25}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d84f3f85-0bac-5714-9144-2e45d672fe35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265128} {:answer/id #uuid "5409c2c8-8bc4-5b80-8688-416d06414c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5409c2c8-8bc4-5b80-8688-416d06414c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265129} :answer-field/id #uuid "49c2262f-6afa-53cb-8968-1218151257cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7014e7be-206b-5dfc-9e20-eaf8d844e0db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7014e7be-206b-5dfc-9e20-eaf8d844e0db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265131} :answer-field/id #uuid "40605da4-386e-554d-858c-68bff1e17dfe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265130}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e153e5a9-f6b6-5107-8a56-e685d6dc9017" :question/math-academy-id "q-316755" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-6+5\\text{i}}{4+7\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $4+7\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $4-7\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $4-7\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6+5\\text{i}}{4+7\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-6+5\\text{i}}{4+7\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{4-7\\text{i}}{4-7\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6+5\\text{i})(4-7\\text{i})}{(4+7\\text{i})(4-7\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24+42\\text{i}+20\\text{i}-35{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{4}^{2}-(7\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24+62\\text{i}-35(-1)}{{4}^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24+62\\text{i}+35}{16+49} \\\\  & =\\frac{11+62\\text{i}}{65}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11+62\\text{i}}{65}=(\\frac{11}{65})+(\\frac{62}{65})\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "138d7477-a3bd-514c-9c83-0a4d1ce00473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "138d7477-a3bd-514c-9c83-0a4d1ce00473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265134} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc9f8cbe-2713-5346-9dc2-369f432263d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa3962eb-9ada-5f54-948c-b122fe607f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa3962eb-9ada-5f54-948c-b122fe607f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265136} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c24b87a-3397-585e-b88a-0a6e2829cd01" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3dd3004a-0a49-58ed-9297-bdbfe14a63c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-316773" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{6+\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$\\,)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6+\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{6+\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-3\\text{i}}{1-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6+\\text{i})(1-3\\text{i})}{(1+3\\text{i})(1-3\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-18\\text{i}+\\text{i}-3{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-17\\text{i}-3(-1)}{1-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-17\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9-17\\text{i}}{10}=(\\frac{9}{10})+(-\\frac{17}{10})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc6c30d1-8ecf-50e6-a66a-0909c2b8f0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc6c30d1-8ecf-50e6-a66a-0909c2b8f0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265139} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6ada72-28bf-5950-a297-c0f517d035b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5fc1cf-968d-5714-a780-e00c0a91b6cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f5fc1cf-968d-5714-a780-e00c0a91b6cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265141} :answer-field/id #uuid "86bdf9c3-c1fb-5167-946d-240bbabbd436" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265140}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e535981f-647e-56d4-8c1b-fdc761659fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316848" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $3-\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3+\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3+\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}} & =\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3+\\text{i}}{3+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\text{i}+7{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\text{i}+7(-1)}{9-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7+21\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+21\\text{i}}{10}=(-\\frac{7}{10})+(\\frac{21}{10})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265142 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8cbecc-c7e5-5e90-9187-28f428f47de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f8cbecc-c7e5-5e90-9187-28f428f47de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265144} :answer-field/id #uuid "91de5d4d-7126-592e-80ef-b5dadaa948be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0e1086-ce08-5fa2-9da9-ae75f8c0bdb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c0e1086-ce08-5fa2-9da9-ae75f8c0bdb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265146} :answer-field/id #uuid "909ad128-2745-53a8-9279-a0e451489ba4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265145}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "610c8180-b5d7-5311-92f5-d44081327a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-316850" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{8\\text{i}}{3-4\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $3-4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3+4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3+4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8\\text{i}}{3-4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{8\\text{i}}{3-4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3+4\\text{i}}{3+4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\text{i}+32{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\text{i}+32(-1)}{9-(-16)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-32+24\\text{i}}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-32+24\\text{i}}{25}=(-\\frac{32}{25})+(\\frac{24}{25})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9661c8aa-1cb0-502a-811a-dae34f2cfbfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9661c8aa-1cb0-502a-811a-dae34f2cfbfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265149} :answer-field/id #uuid "34939488-77e3-59a8-a8fa-c76fdafe6fa9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265148} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62964329-b2f4-5a95-a1d9-6811ee98575c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62964329-b2f4-5a95-a1d9-6811ee98575c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265151} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dab066d-a047-5ce1-a749-55b5bab66d53" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265150}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "606bfe8f-4958-5895-90ba-a80a3efde597" :question/math-academy-id "q-316861" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{3}{1+2\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{3}{1+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-2\\text{i}}{1-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-2\\text{i})}{{1}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6\\text{i}}{1-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6\\text{i}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3-6\\text{i}}{5}=(\\frac{3}{5})+(-\\frac{6}{5})\\,\\text{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5f64e38-476b-5f65-a7ab-97688bdce75a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265154} {:answer/id #uuid "b3739184-204b-5bf6-b778-a2d5a444aeea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3739184-204b-5bf6-b778-a2d5a444aeea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265155} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6aa6ee7-e372-51d5-8ba2-ae0d45a38ced" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdeec6d9-b946-53ac-95bc-5c5a92c0252c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdeec6d9-b946-53ac-95bc-5c5a92c0252c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265157} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ba8ffbe-dc66-569c-b582-03aace0c758d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265156}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2efc6690-2ef4-56f4-8d72-5a314a4a1df0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316883" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{9-5\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $6\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+6\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-6\\text{i},$ or simply $-6\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-6\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9-5\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}} & =\\frac{9-5\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-6\\text{i}}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-54\\text{i}+30{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-36{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-54\\text{i}+30(-1)}{-36(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-30-54\\text{i}}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-30-54\\text{i}}{36} & =-\\frac{30}{36}-\\frac{54}{36}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{5}{6})+(-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b81daf5f-e51c-51d3-bfaf-983a1184bc78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b81daf5f-e51c-51d3-bfaf-983a1184bc78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265160} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d45df6c-3419-51e4-b80f-354626e3acba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da14f780-82e1-5dfa-9aa8-4516f3fb928c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da14f780-82e1-5dfa-9aa8-4516f3fb928c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265162} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cb2c6d4-24e6-5409-8036-856ee45b04e0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265161}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5fd3fcca-a299-5ed3-acd7-f31b57fee4ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-316885" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-4+9\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $6\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+6\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-6\\text{i},$ or simply $-6\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-6\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4+9\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-4+9\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-6\\text{i}}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\text{i}-54{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-36{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\text{i}-54(-1)}{-36(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{54+24\\text{i}}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{54+24\\text{i}}{36} & =\\frac{54}{36}+\\frac{24}{36}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2})+(\\frac{2}{3})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cb402d8-5cef-5c13-af7d-a60cd743f2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb402d8-5cef-5c13-af7d-a60cd743f2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265165} :answer-field/id #uuid "f924ba43-9f57-5d41-80d0-ee5851ea78fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "971980d3-5327-544b-a860-bdb8142b4fe4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "971980d3-5327-544b-a860-bdb8142b4fe4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265167} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ee273e-74c6-55b3-9903-941db30a291d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265166}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "316b450f-4d16-5f0f-a3da-b6e3a2ee9dde" :question/math-academy-id "q-316887" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-9+7\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}=($\n {{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $8\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+8\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-8\\text{i},$ or simply $-8\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-8\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-9+7\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-9+7\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-8\\text{i}}{-8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{72\\text{i}-56{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-64{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{72\\text{i}-56(-1)}{-64(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{56+72\\text{i}}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{56+72\\text{i}}{64} & =\\frac{56}{64}+\\frac{72}{64}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{7}{8})+(\\frac{9}{8})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3d07014-7e8e-53aa-82ac-fd1ad5f5fcc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{21}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265170} {:answer/id #uuid "970c3f19-13ef-59e5-8b7e-e909ac89d3f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "970c3f19-13ef-59e5-8b7e-e909ac89d3f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265171} :answer-field/id #uuid "27d11b5d-40e5-5da5-9787-94fbde9d9679" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86c4da34-9aea-5cb7-a74f-a178e578eec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86c4da34-9aea-5cb7-a74f-a178e578eec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265173} :answer-field/id #uuid "116de029-729f-5e18-ace5-55b50491e436" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265172}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6fb791e3-fb32-5231-9d41-86934a0474c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-316893" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{7}{3-4\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $3-4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3+4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3+4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3-4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{7}{3-4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3+4\\text{i}}{3+4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21+28\\text{i}}{9+12\\text{i}-12\\text{i}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21+28\\text{i}}{9-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{21+28\\text{i}}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{21}{25}+\\frac{28}{25}\\text{i}=(\\frac{21}{25})+(\\frac{28}{25})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e06102ba-d71c-501a-bbe5-5231fdbe2f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{21}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e06102ba-d71c-501a-bbe5-5231fdbe2f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{21}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265176} :answer-field/id #uuid "41ab8a6e-bfed-5878-99c2-3122cd58c6b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265175} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bb47119-633c-5814-a235-93d32c34a302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bb47119-633c-5814-a235-93d32c34a302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265178} :answer-field/id #uuid "e91efde3-49b2-593e-b14d-568da7ac93b3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265177}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d0216a7-e3c0-5c91-81a4-68e9a0db0e49" :question/math-academy-id "q-316896" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{7}{-3-2\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-3-2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-3+2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3+2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{-3-2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{7}{-3-2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3+2\\text{i}}{-3+2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(-3+2\\text{i})}{(-3)^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-21+14\\text{i}}{9-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-21+14\\text{i}}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-21+14\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{21}{13})+(\\frac{14}{13})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c37ba39-e719-5983-9ff5-f6447f7e974e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265181} {:answer/id #uuid "69274d97-1df3-54e5-a65e-c988603ba447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c37ba39-e719-5983-9ff5-f6447f7e974e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265181} :answer-field/id #uuid "095e16a8-3a79-5cc1-b77c-c18462414596" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bdc5b66-6608-56d4-bd89-df374350f4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bdc5b66-6608-56d4-bd89-df374350f4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265184} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed86f562-7f92-581c-8aba-9ee39c907bd9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265183}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1599423c-9248-5ffa-9d17-823c2bf2328f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316904" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(5+2\\text{i})(-2+3\\text{i})}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+15\\text{i}-4\\text{i}+6{\\text{i}}^{2}}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+11\\text{i}+6(-1)}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{16}{13})+(\\frac{11}{13})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f440557-d087-5155-afd1-7ceb42834f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265187} {:answer/id #uuid "f390a28f-3d53-5253-99cf-06bb22133c3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5+\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265188} {:answer/id #uuid "82fb813c-495a-5b23-8f49-feccf0d345c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1+\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265189} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7dbe76-76cd-50f4-8eb3-a0cb9cac1201" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265190} {:answer/id #uuid "173e402b-3348-54a4-858f-b7ecfcbc646e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "173e402b-3348-54a4-858f-b7ecfcbc646e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265191} :answer-field/id #uuid "15e21387-ea93-5735-ad3b-65eaf9eecfeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265186}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f68bfa55-213f-510b-8d57-1979ae37022b" :question/math-academy-id "q-555" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\text{i}}{2-\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $2-\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $2+\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2+\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{i}}{2-\\text{i}} & =\\frac{\\text{i}}{2-\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{2+\\text{i}}{2+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\text{i}+{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{2}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+2\\text{i}}{{2}^{2}-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+2\\text{i}}{4+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+2\\text{i}}{5}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1+2\\text{i}}{5}=-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19ff6e3a-a94f-5430-a9a9-d940c8251d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}-\\frac{11}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265194} {:answer/id #uuid "1e890b79-f123-56bb-bcb6-694d4de346d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{11}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265195} {:answer/id #uuid "e6895bbb-0ef0-5273-90f0-fefce543b7fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}+\\frac{11}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265196} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6ad37a-62c7-59a9-a400-42923d0478fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}+\\frac{11}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265197} {:answer/id #uuid "8e22a568-2478-5da3-a7c7-65f68c1d464c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}-\\frac{11}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19ff6e3a-a94f-5430-a9a9-d940c8251d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}-\\frac{11}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265194} :answer-field/id #uuid "f49a89d0-e64e-5fce-a104-773446256cb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8c9fe5f-f092-5b94-8f94-9f25e87326f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74611" :question/problem "if ${z}_{1}=3-5\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=1+2\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3-5\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $1+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{3-5\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-5\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-2\\text{i}}{1-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6\\text{i}-5\\text{i}+10{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{2}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-11\\text{i}+10(-1)}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-11\\text{i}-10}{1+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7-11\\text{i}}{5}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-7-11\\text{i}}{5}=-\\frac{7}{5}-\\frac{11}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ea40a87-7ac7-5a06-a315-d9d42d2673c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265201} {:answer/id #uuid "fd63e245-b528-5199-94f9-90d4c86516f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265202} {:answer/id #uuid "540a41e6-50fa-5958-ac63-d6c032921ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-6\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265203} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a68d5a-095d-5f60-9ae2-247cb33372aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265204} {:answer/id #uuid "3544e49d-f4bc-5777-987e-bcc9db30e2eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7a68d5a-095d-5f60-9ae2-247cb33372aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265204} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d676989-8ff2-504e-89b8-448c2c534fe9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265200}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3fdd8cb6-8ee8-5a9d-9cde-78122b06d1eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-74644" :question/problem "$\\frac{15\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{15\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-2\\text{i}}{1-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\text{i}-30{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{2}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\text{i}-30(-1)}{1-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\text{i}+30}{1+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{30+15\\text{i}}{5}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{30+15\\text{i}}{5}=\\frac{30}{5}+\\frac{15}{5}\\text{i}=6+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bea7014a-2ec7-5bc1-9286-c1ed2aadf3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{13}-\\frac{27}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265208} {:answer/id #uuid "917b6f05-edd5-53dc-8a8e-3a94bc2e3f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{13}+\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265209} {:answer/id #uuid "25ea1f31-37a2-55c3-8cca-9c788a9e0c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}+\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265210} {:answer/id #uuid "25e30022-e454-5b13-933e-a1a0a68b584c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265211} {:answer/id #uuid "50a4f5be-7f4f-5da6-b15b-e24fe8e99cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50a4f5be-7f4f-5da6-b15b-e24fe8e99cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265212} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfdf262a-8a69-5f89-9cb7-40b82cfbac0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265207}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ca3346d-d2b9-53ea-9f84-d9305b392ee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74648" :question/problem "$\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-3+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-3-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3-2\\text{i}}{-3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+6\\text{i}-6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}=-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3ae78aa-a8ba-5371-9a04-15acfd48b66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265215} {:answer/id #uuid "15b6bed4-902c-5c4e-becf-c810855b2013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265216} {:answer/id #uuid "b3423c26-80ab-5b46-b4b5-59bfd96f259c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265217} {:answer/id #uuid "c4eabb36-f6b3-577e-9d33-49b95f12f027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265218} {:answer/id #uuid "f147c615-f613-5bfb-ac8f-6df935875467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3423c26-80ab-5b46-b4b5-59bfd96f259c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265217} :answer-field/id #uuid "e48681cf-2d37-5061-9ef2-e8325e724d7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265214}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b1df748-6885-5736-937a-15d2623e818b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74659" :question/problem "If ${z}_{1}=1-12\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=8\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $8\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+8\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-8\\text{i},$ or simply $-8\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-8\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-8\\text{i}}{-8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+96{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-64{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+96(-1)}{-64(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-96-8\\text{i}}{64}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-96-8\\text{i}}{64}=-\\frac{96}{64}-\\frac{8}{64}\\text{i}=-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "957eb747-c786-5ed5-81c6-9a7d97b49d39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265222} {:answer/id #uuid "383ddaa4-1324-50dc-80df-87b3797aaabf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265223} {:answer/id #uuid "c75f51c1-ee9a-5c57-97cd-fbf43cef63d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265224} {:answer/id #uuid "36b6a57f-5bf8-531f-8f53-aad77bd337dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265225} {:answer/id #uuid "37352a9b-5a04-5720-a017-28037f8a75a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "957eb747-c786-5ed5-81c6-9a7d97b49d39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265222} :answer-field/id #uuid "55b6a45f-2eab-57dd-ad5e-70e2ef9d6fe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265221}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7d5daa6-e06b-50a9-a8f7-655d6e8baf26" :question/math-academy-id "q-962" :question/problem "$\\frac{5}{6+2\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $6+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $6-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $6-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{6+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5}{6+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{6-2\\text{i}}{6-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-10\\text{i}}{36-12\\text{i}+12\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-10\\text{i}}{36-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-10\\text{i}}{36-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-10\\text{i}}{36+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-10\\text{i}}{40}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{30-10\\text{i}}{40}=\\frac{30}{40}-\\frac{10}{40}\\text{i}=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
